<!--meta {"lead": "A switch turns a setting on or off immediately, with no save button: email updates about requests, a reminder the day before an appointment.", "description": "On/off switch with label right or left and an optional description; every state in both themes.", "pills": ["<code>role=\"switch\"</code> on a checkbox", "Status: core set"], "variants": "label right, label left (settings row), with description", "states": "off, on, hover, focus, disabled", "sources": ["pages/account-settings/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a switch for a setting that takes effect the moment it changes, like notification preferences in account settings. If the change only applies after "Save changes", use a <a href="checkbox.html">checkbox</a> instead; the cookie-preferences dialog, which saves on "Save preferences", correctly uses a checkbox. Its home is the notification preferences card in account settings.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Email me when Nia replies</span></label>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 10%; top: 22%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 22%; top: 72%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 58%; top: 22%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Track</b><small>44 × 24px pill; <code>--color-border-strong</code> off, <code>--color-accent</code> on.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Thumb</b><small>20px circle in the surface colour with <code>--shadow-1</code>; slides 20px.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Label</b><small>Names the setting, not the action.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack,start]Label right (inline), and label left in a settings row (<code>.switch--end</code>) with a description.}}
<label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Email me when Nia replies</span></label>
<div class="card" style="width: 100%;"><label class="switch switch--end"><input type="checkbox" role="switch"><span class="choice__text"><span>Appointment reminders</span><small class="text-muted">A text the day before Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am.</small></span></label></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="Switches have one size: a 44 × 24px track in a row at least 24px tall."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Disabled</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Off</th>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch"><span>Reminders</span></label></td>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" data-state="hover"><span>Reminders</span></label></td>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" data-state="focus"><span>Reminders</span></label></td>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" disabled><span>Reminders</span></label></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">On</th>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Reminders</span></label></td>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked data-state="hover"><span>Reminders</span></label></td>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked data-state="focus"><span>Reminders</span></label></td>
        <td><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked disabled><span>Reminders</span></label></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>A switch has no invalid state: it cannot be wrong. If saving the change fails, flip it back and say so in a toast ("Reminders not updated. Try again.").</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Email updates</span></label><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch"><span>Reminders</span></label>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>In settings lists the switch sits at the end of a full-width row (<code>.switch--end</code>), so labels align on the left. The label keeps at least 10em beside the switch; when it cannot (a narrow card, 200% text) the switch wraps beneath the label at the start instead of pushing the label off the card. The DOM order stays input, then text.</li>
    <li>Descriptions wrap under the label; the switch stays vertically centred while it shares the row.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Component tokens: <code>--switch-track</code> (<code>--color-border-strong</code>), <code>--switch-track-on</code> (<code>--color-accent</code>), <code>--switch-thumb-bg</code> (<code>--color-bg-surface</code>), and the sizes <code>--switch-width</code>, <code>--switch-height</code> and <code>--switch-thumb</code>. In dark the thumb is grey 900 on a plum 300 track.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p><code>&lt;input type="checkbox" role="switch"&gt;</code> inside its label: screen readers announce "switch, on/off". See the <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/switch/">APG Switch pattern</a>.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Focuses the switch.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Toggles it; the change applies immediately.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared ring follows the track's pill shape.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The label names the setting ("Appointment reminders"), never the action ("Turn on reminders"), so "on" and "off" read correctly. Confirm the saved change in a polite live region.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Off track on card|--color-border-strong|--color-bg-surface|3}}
    {{pair:Thumb on off track|--color-bg-surface|--color-border-strong|3}}
    {{pair:Thumb on on track|--color-bg-surface|--color-accent|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Forced colours</h3>
  <p>System colours would erase the track and thumb backgrounds, so the switch sets its own: a <code>CanvasText</code> hairline edge on the track and a <code>CanvasText</code> thumb; on, the track is <code>Highlight</code> with a <code>HighlightText</code> thumb (<code>forced-color-adjust: none</code>). The focus ring maps to <code>Highlight</code>.</p>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>The thumb slides and the track recolours over <code>--duration-base</code> (200ms); reduced motion makes both instant. Position, not just colour, shows the state.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>The whole label row toggles the switch; the track alone is 44px wide.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Labels are nouns for settings: "Email updates", "Appointment reminders".</li>
    <li>Descriptions say what "on" means with real detail: "A text the day before Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am."</li>
    <li>Do not add "On" / "Off" text beside the switch; the role announces it.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Appointment reminders</span></label></div><figcaption>A setting that saves as soon as it flips.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="stack stack--sm"><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Remember my optional usage choices</span></label><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Save preferences</button></div></div><figcaption>A switch inside the cookie dialog, which only applies on "Save preferences". Keep the checkbox the mock uses.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch"><span>Email updates</span></label></div><figcaption>Name the setting.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch"><span>Turn off email updates</span></label></div><figcaption>An action label makes "on" mean "off".</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Track, off|--color-border-strong}}
      {{tok:Track, off hover|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Track, on|--color-accent}}
      {{tok:Thumb|--color-bg-surface}}
      {{tok:Thumb shadow|--shadow-1}}
      {{tok:Thumb inset|--space-0-5}}
      {{tok:Radius|--radius-full}}
      {{tok:Slide|--duration-base|--ease-standard}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;label class="switch switch--end"&gt;
  &lt;input type="checkbox" role="switch" name="reminders" checked&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;Appointment reminders&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/label&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.switch</code></td><td>Track, thumb and label row.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.switch--end</code></td><td>Full-width settings row, switch at the end; wraps beneath the label when the label would have less than 10em.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>role="switch"</code></td><td>Announced as a switch.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>checked</code> / <code>disabled</code></td><td>On / disabled.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|focus|checked|disabled"</code></td><td>Documentation only.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Core-set component. Its look comes from the mocks' kit (<code>.switch</code>); account settings uses it for notification preferences that save as soon as they change.</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/default|notification preferences: settings rows with descriptions}}
    {{mock:dialogs/cookie-preferences/default|correctly a checkbox, not a switch}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: the kit's switch had no hover state and no <code>role="switch"</code> in its markup; the thumb travel was a raw 1.25rem (now computed from the component tokens); the <code>row-reverse</code> settings row pushed a long label off the card at 200% text (now it wraps); the on switch vanished in forced colours (now it has its own forced-colours rules).</p>
</section>
